<div id="2026-11-18-reviewer-repo-facts" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-18 — Commit reviewer blocked on files that already exist</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> A commit was blocked with a <em>high</em> finding: <code>ReviewRun.pm:28</code> uses <code>Comserv::Util::AI::ReviewGate</code>, "a module that is not in this diff … if it is not committed, CodeReviewer and everything that loads it fail to compile." The module was already committed (HEAD <code>ea49509b5</code>) and loads; it is missing from the diff only because nothing in it changed. A second finding claimed mojibake in a changelog entry that contains no byte above <code>0x7f</code>. Both were invented from a blind spot, and the fail-closed gate turned the first one into a blocked commit.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> <code>CodeReviewer::build_messages</code> sends system prompt, task and diff — nothing else. The model cannot tell "not in this diff" from "does not exist in the repo", so absence from the diff was reported as absence from the repository. No prompt wording fixes that; it needs facts.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix.</strong> <code>Admin::Git::_repo_module_note</code> collects every module named by an added <code>use</code>/<code>require</code> line, drops core modules and pragmas via <code>Module::CoreList</code>, then reports which of the rest exist at <code>lib/&lt;Module&gt;.pm</code> and which do not. Both reviewer call sites pass it as <code>repo_note</code>; <code>ReviewRun</code> forwards it to <code>build_messages</code>, which renders a "Repository facts" block and tells the reviewer not to report repo-present files as missing. An empty diff (or a core-only diff) adds no block, so prompts do not grow for ordinary commits.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/AI/ReviewRun.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/AI/CodeReviewer.pm</code></p>
</div>
